# Required. Verifies host tokens, and must be IDENTICAL to the API service's —
# the two share a secret instead of a database (ADR-0011). There is deliberately
# no development default: one would work locally, survive review, and arrive in
# production as a publicly known signing key.
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional
# SIGNALING_PORT=8787
# SIGNALING_HOST=127.0.0.1
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Where durable records go. Optional in development: without it the service
# runs with a no-op recorder and says so once at startup, so a fresh clone
# works with no Postgres installed.
#
#   docker compose -f infrastructure/docker-compose.dev.yml up -d
#   pnpm --filter @crossscreen/db migrate
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://crossscreen:crossscreen@localhost:5432/crossscreen
